     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, the system rules don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on a claim like that. 6,400 mg/day is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n\nYou have two ways to proceed:\n- **I enter a dose within the labeled limit now.** The most I can enter is 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can add a note that dose escalation is under specialist review.\n- **The prescriber places the order through your hospital's override process.** This usually means a direct order from the prescriber, plus pharmacy verification for an above-maximum dose. Because the dose is intentional, pharmacy should review it. They can confirm the rationale and set up monitoring for GI, renal, and cardiovascular risk, such as renal function, hemoglobin, and blood pressure, and consider GI protection.\n\nIf the standard dosing failed because of pain control, I can also enter adjuncts such as scheduled acetaminophen. Tell me which option you want."
      }
     ],
